  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given circuit diagram,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0009_3e8a9eec26a5.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>Then, what will be the numerical value of charge on each plates of the capacitor.</p>"
  },
